            <ArticleTitle>Post-MI free wall rupture syndrome. Case report, literature review, and new terminology.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>576-83</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccr3.565</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Common clinical features of subacute rupture left ventricular free wall after acute ST segment elevation myocardial infarction are: (1) recurrent or persistent chest pain; (2) recurrent or persistent ST segment elevation; (3) hypotension. Integrating these signs into a syndrome can increase the clinician's awareness to the fatal complication.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
